<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Maximum speed and distance between stages</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>A matatu leaves a stage from rest and stops at the next stage \({@Tend@}\) seconds later. Its velocity \(t\) seconds after it leaves is \(v = {@kk@}t({@Tend@} - t)\) m/s.</p><p>(a) Find its greatest speed.</p><div>Greatest speed \(=\) [[input:ans1]] m/s [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the distance between the two stages.</p><div>Distance \(=\) [[input:ans2]] m [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>Differentiate to find when the speed is greatest; integrate to find the distance.</p><p>(a) \(\dfrac{dv}{dt} = {@diff(vt,t)@} = 0\) when \(t = {@thalf@}\). Then \(v = {@kk@} \times {@thalf@} \times {@thalf@} = {@vmax@}\) m/s.</p><p>(b) The velocity is never negative, so the distance is \(\displaystyle\int_0^{ {@Tend@} } {@kk@}t({@Tend@} - t)\,dt = \left[{@integrate(expand(vt),t)@}\right]_0^{ {@Tend@} } = {@dist@}\) m.</p><p>This is \(\tfrac{2}{3}\) of top speed \(\times\) time: more than the triangle \(\tfrac{1}{2} \times {@Tend@} \times {@vmax@}\) and less than the rectangle \({@Tend@} \times {@vmax@}\).</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>2</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: [T, vmax]: v = k t (T - t) with k = 4 vmax / T^2, a unit fraction on every entry. Source: original. */
L: [[30,9],[36,9],[42,9],[48,9],[48,16],[60,12],[66,9],[84,14],[90,15],[96,12]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
Tend: L[ix][1]; vmax: L[ix][2];
kk: 4*vmax/Tend^2;
vt: kk*t*(Tend-t);
dist: ev(integrate(vt, t, 0, Tend));
/* diagnostics */
thalf: Tend/2;
rect: vmax*Tend;
tri: vmax*Tend/2;]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
